{
  "walkthrough": [
    "Goal: the kinds whose answer is built from given parts, a value scale, a box to complete, free boxes and an ellipse, practised in one frame, the one I draw in; what the exercise gives printed in it in a grey I cannot take for my own ink or pencil; and Compare showing the answer laid over my drawing (a scale's uneven cells outlined, a drawn copy judged by my eye, S145), the way to see it (看画法) one tap away (the author, 2026-10-30: the original's frame only repeated the question, a box's Compare was cluttered with every stroke drawn on dashed, an edge drawn twice drawn on twice, and a value scale's How fitted 5 cells while the row had up to 7).",
    "Entry (S101: the test crops imported first, so a combination copies a crop): lessons from the home, each its kind's: Value scales at level 1 (two scales of five cells), Boxes at level 1, Ellipses at level 1, Value scales at level 3 (nine cells, of a hue), Free boxes at level 1; Home between them leaves each under way.",
    "Value scale, my first: five cells (a beginner's level; the third level's are nine), the dark and light ends filled as given in the one frame; the frame beside it, where the original lay, is empty. Its How shows by itself, its example as many cells as my row (S97's review: a five-cell row read against a nine-cell example's 'the 5th' confused the author): five cells in other colours than mine, its order numbered 2 1 2 under its inner cells, the middle cell painted first, then each half's middle, each round its step lit; then Compare's marks: the even row under the copy's, cell under cell, one uneven cell outlined red with its even one. Steps: the middle cell first (the 3rd), then the middle of each half (the 2nd and 4th); Compare.",
    "I pick values on the wheel moving only up and down and tap Fill cell three times: the cells fill one after another. Compare: under my row the even scale, cell under cell; the middle cell, too dark, outlined red together with its even one; the card its title and '1 cell uneven.' (no bars any more). Compare again takes it away; a lighter value, the pen touching the middle cell (S100: it takes it in hand and paints nothing, a scale has no pens) and Fill cell, Compare: every cell even, the card its title alone.",
    "Box: one frame, the horizon labelled and the front corner with its three edges printed in slate grey; the original's slot empty. Its How by itself: ghost each edge, draw it once, a wrong one redrawn once with Correct, never scratched over, an edge checked by running it on in pencil; its example's Compare the red box with its hidden edges dashed, its points ringed, over the ink (S145). I sketch a construction line, draw the nine edges with Draw (one bottom edge a little off) and redraw another a few pixels and a degree off it, as a hand does.",
    "Compare: the exact box red over mine, see-through and as thick as the pen, its hidden edges dashed; its two vanishing points ringed red on the sheet beside the frame, one in the empty slot; nothing of my edges is read or marked: the edge drawn off stands apart from the red. The card: 'Box 1', Construction, How close is it?, Accurate, Almost, Again. Construction tapped: faint grey lines from every corner of the red box to both points and the horizon run on across the sheet, the word in the ink pill; tapped again: gone. The correcting pen redraws the off edge (the comparison goes as it lands); Compare: the red over my correction, Construction off again; I choose Almost.",
    "Ellipse: its frame printed grey in the one frame. I draw it a little narrow and to the left. Compare: the exact ellipse red over mine, nothing fitted or ringed; the card Construction and the eye's three; Construction: the frame's diagonals and middle lines faint, the four middles dotted; tapped again, gone. I choose Accurate.",
    "Home, then a lesson of Value scales at level 3: nine cells now, of a hue. How, tapped: its example nine cells too, numbered 3 2 3 1 3 2 3, steps the middle cell (the 5th), the middle of each half (the 3rd and 7th), the cells left (the 2nd, 4th, 6th and 8th), Compare; Got it. I touch its middle cell, then the 3rd and the 7th, with the pen and fill each with Fill cell (S100), my values picked carelessly; Compare: the nine-cell even row under mine, my three cells each outlined red with its even one, '3 cells uneven.', the cells I left bare nothing, and no result while cells are bare. Then Home and a lesson of Free boxes: the horizon alone printed in the frame, no example box. I draw three boxes, one edge turned off and one box with a narrow front corner.",
    "Compare: the horizon run on faint across the sheet and nothing else: no ring, no arc, no line read from my boxes; the card the eye's three, no Construction. I choose Accurate. Finish: the summary.",
    "Levels (S142), the same lessons in Chinese: a long box at 熟练, a box drawn through at 稳 compared (准, 差一点, 重来), a turned frame among 稳's ellipses, the How cards 自由盒子：仰视 and 自由盒子：俯视 with their steps (第三个消失点), the guided page looking up and the bare page looking down compared, its horizon run on, 差一点 chosen.",
    "In Chinese (this file, s97-one-frame run as on a Chinese tablet): 看画法, '1 格不均匀。', 准, 差一点, 重来, the How cards' new words; the steps and the canvas's hashes are s97-one-frame's.",
    "Not here: stage 3's tricks and solids and stage 4's objects (S98); a sheet made before 1.15.0 reopened (the store's upgrade, its scale kept by its seed: `store/src/practice_tests.rs`); the author's hand on the tablet."
